    <!-- ===================== Icon geometry =====================
         Phosphor (https://phosphoricons.com), MIT - see Assets/ICONS-LICENSE.txt.

         Chosen over the obvious sets for two reasons. Its terminals are rounded, which is what
         the wordmark is made of, so the icons and the logo look like they come from the same
         hand. And it is not derived from Feather, unlike Lucide and Tabler - which is what
         every other product on the shelf is wearing.

         Drawn on a 256 grid as filled shapes rather than strokes. Filled reads better small: a
         hairline outline at fifteen pixels on a shop machine's screen turns to grey mush, where
         a solid shape keeps its silhouette.

         Converted, not copied: WPF Geometry has no circle, rect, line or polyline, so each of
         those is rewritten as arcs and lines with Phosphor's own coordinates. Nothing in this
         file was drawn by hand. -->

